    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i guess. but even the \"rituals\" idea feels like i'm just dragging out a sentence that should have ended already. like, if you're truly at the end of your rope, why would you bother journaling? it's just more noise. there's this feeling that for a story to be real, it has to be honest about the finality of things. if elias just keeps \"struggling through,\" it feels like i'm denying him the only thing that actually makes sense for him: just letting go. it's hard to write about a character when you know that staying is just a slower way of suffering. don't you think a story loses its truth if it refuses to let a character find an actual exit?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
